::kind(writ)

==[ type-purity ]

@rule(type-purity){
  guard: { twrit: pure }

  pure: {
    crates: [ "crates/tomet-base-type" ]
    forbid: [ "std::fs", "std::net", "std::process", "std::env" ]
    allow-external: []
  }
}

`tomet-type` is a pure, side-effect-free base-layer crate representing the type
vocabulary. It performs no I/O and holds zero external dependencies.
Layering rules in the root `.writ.tmt` govern that Layer 1 crates depend on no
other workspace crates.
